            <div xml:id="d682">

                <pb facs="1920" n="1746" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v10-12mSupp/pg1746"/>

                <head>682. Memorandum from U. Alexis Johnson to McGeorge Bundy, May 27, enclosing a
                    memorandum entitled “Possible Soviet Initiatives To End U.S. Aerial
                    Reconnaissance Over Cuba”<anchor n="1" xml:id="d682-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1963-05-27">May 27, 1963</date>
                    </dateline></opener>
                <pb facs="d682-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d682-1"/>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Memorandum for the NSC Standing Group on Possible Soviet Initiatives to
                        End US Aerial Reconnaissance over Cuba</item>
                </list>
                <p>Enclosed is a memorandum which Paul Nitze and I have prepared to examine the
                    question of possible Communist initiatives against our <pb facs="1921" n="1747"
                        type="typeset" xml:id="pg1747"/> aerial reconnaissance, particularly short
                    of shooting down a U–2. We would address the question whether at this time, or
                    under what conditions, the Communists would decide that the need for action was
                    so imperative that they would undertake one or more of those courses of
                    action.</p>
                <p>As in the case of earlier contingency studies with respect to Cuba, while we have
                    used few members of our staffs this memorandum has not been fully staffed in
                    either State or DOD nor seen by the JCS, and thus does not necessary represent
                    the views of our respective Departments. Also, we are presenting this study in
                    accordance with the desires of the Standing Group merely to provide a basis for
                    discussion.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>U. Alexis Johnson</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d682-a1.xml" xpointer="d682-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
